<%# The loading skeleton of an entry card. Each collection of entries uses it. It has the same %>
<%# shape as an entry summary: an eyebrow, a heading, and `lines` lines of body text. %>
<%# Give `lines:` for the size of the body: an event needs 4, and a summary needs 2, which is %>
<%# the default. %>
<% line_count = defined?(lines) ? lines : 2 %>
<%# The container tags are the same as in the _summary card of the api, which replaces this. Thus a
<%# selector such as
    `article.entry` or `header.entry__header` in the jointly-owned _entry.scss reach both.
    ⚠️ The heading stays a span, deliberately: an empty h3 would announce a nameless heading. %>
<article class="entry entry--summary">
  <header class="entry__header">
    <p class="entry__meta"><wa-skeleton class="entry-skeleton-eyebrow" effect="sheen"></wa-skeleton></p>
    <span class="entry__hed"><wa-skeleton class="entry-skeleton-heading" effect="sheen"></wa-skeleton></span>
  </header>
  <div class="entry__body">
    <% line_count.times do %>
      <wa-skeleton class="entry-skeleton-line" effect="sheen"></wa-skeleton>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</article>
